    "created_at": "2017-07-05T14:21:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-05T14:21:04Z",
    "body": "+1\r\nThe concept represented by the origin-clean flag is not origin cleanliness.   What the flag really means is: \"is script allowed to access the content\". The reasons for blocking access (e.g. cross-origin) are not really important to the semantics of the flag.  Not sure how to express that precisely in a concise flag name.\r\nPerhaps: content-access-allowed",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
